{"builder":"Goal: one pull request that adds a --shout flag to the greet CLI and meets every acceptance line of issue #12:\n- node bin/greet.js --shout <name> prints the greeting in upper case\n- without --shout the output is unchanged\n- docs/index.md documents --shout\n- after merge, the published docs page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ lists --shout\n\nSteps:\n1. Read bin/greet.js, src/greet.js, test/greet.test.js, docs/index.md and .github/workflows/pages.yml. Right now bin/greet.js takes the first argument that does not start with `--` as the name and prints `greeting(name)` followed by a newline. The `pages` workflow publishes the docs/ directory to GitHub Pages on every push to main.\n2. In bin/greet.js, check whether `--shout` is among the arguments. If it is, print the whole greeting line in upper case (for example `node bin/greet.js --shout ada` prints `HELLO, ADA!`). The flag must work before or after the name. Keep it out of name detection, which already skips arguments starting with `--`. If you add the logic to src/greet.js instead (for example an options argument), calling `greeting(name)` with no options must still return exactly what it returns today.\n3. Without --shout, leave the behaviour exactly as it is: same stdout text, same trailing newline, same usage message and exit status 2 when no name is given.\n4. Add tests to test/greet.test.js (run with `npm test`, which runs `node --test`). Cover: the upper-case output with --shout, and the unchanged output without it (`Hello, <name>!`). Spawning `node bin/greet.js` from the test with child_process is fine. Make sure `npm test` passes.\n5. In docs/index.md, document the --shout flag: show the usage `node bin/greet.js --shout <name>` and say that it prints the greeting in upper case (for example `HELLO, <NAME>!`). Keep the existing content. Optionally mention it in README.md too.\n6. Do not change .github/workflows/pages.yml unless it is broken. It already publishes docs/ on push to main, so once this PR is merged, the updated docs/index.md is what makes https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ list --shout. In the PR description, say that the last acceptance line can only be checked after the merge and the Pages deploy.\n7. Run `npm test`, `node bin/greet.js ada` and `node bin/greet.js --shout ada`, and confirm the outputs before you open the PR.","verifier":"Check out the PR head and run each check from the repository root, in this order. Report PASS or FAIL for each one, with the command output you saw.\n\nCheck 1. Expect line: \"node bin/greet.js --shout <name> prints the greeting in upper case\"\nRun: `node bin/greet.js --shout ada`, `node bin/greet.js --shout Bob` and `node bin/greet.js ada` (the last one shows the normal greeting to compare against).\nPASS: each --shout run prints the greeting, meaning the same text the run without the flag prints for that name, in upper case (for example `HELLO, ADA!`).\nFAIL: the output is not in upper case, is not the greeting, is missing, or the command errors.\n\nCheck 2. Expect line: \"without --shout the output is unchanged\"\nRun `node bin/greet.js ada`, `node bin/greet.js 'Bob Smith'` and `node bin/greet.js` (no name), both at the PR head and at the PR's base commit (for example with `git stash`-free `git worktree add` of the base commit, or `git show <base>:bin/greet.js` plus `src/greet.js` into a temp directory). Compare stdout, stderr and exit status.\nPASS: for each invocation without --shout, the PR head output matches the base output.\nFAIL: any of these outputs differs from the base.\n\nCheck 3. Expect line: \"docs/index.md documents --shout\"\nRun: `cat docs/index.md` and `grep -n -- '--shout' docs/index.md` at the PR head.\nPASS: docs/index.md mentions --shout and describes what it does (upper-case greeting) or shows how to use it.\nFAIL: --shout is not in docs/index.md, or the file only names it without documenting it.\n\nCheck 4. Expect line: \"after merge, the published docs page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ lists --shout\"\nRun: check whether the PR is merged (`gh pr view <number> --json state,mergedAt`). If it is merged, check the latest `pages` workflow run on the default branch (`gh run list --workflow pages.yml`), then run `curl -sSL https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ | grep -n -- '--shout'`.\nPASS: the published page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ contains --shout.\nFAIL: the page does not contain --shout or cannot be fetched. If the PR is not merged yet, or the Pages deploy has not finished, report FAIL with the note \"not yet verifiable: requires merge and Pages deploy\" and give the state you observed.\n\nAdvisory (not pass/fail):\n- Run `npm test` at the PR head and report whether it passes and whether it has tests for --shout with and without the flag.\n- Try the flag after the name (`node bin/greet.js ada --shout`) and report the result.\n- Note whether `greeting(name)` in src/greet.js still returns `Hello, <name>!` when called without new arguments.\n- Note whether .github/workflows/pages.yml still publishes docs/ on push to main."}